    {
      "name": "Shopify",
      "description": "# Advanced\n***Shopify InPost Lockers & Pickup Points App***<br>\nFor Shopify Advanced Plan, Shopify Plan with Annual Billing or Monthly Fee\n\nPlease contact InPost commercial team to activate the service and receive API credentials.\n\n## Checkout Preview\n\n- List available at the Checkout (No Map)\n- Customers choose Lockers or Pickup Point before the payment\n- Possibility to add Map od List after the Checkout\n- Price for Lockers and Pickup Point can be different\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_1.png\">\n\n\n## Installation and Configuration\n\nInstall the Plugin from this link: https://apps.shopify.com/inpost-3\n\n### 1. Checkout & Payments Settings on Shopify\n\n***Automatically record payments*** <br>\nApp settings and sales channels \u2192 Payments \u2192 Payment capture method \u2192 Select \"Automatically at checkout\"\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_1.png\">\n\n***Make email / full name / phone entry mandatory*** <br>\nApp Settings & Sales Channels \u2192 Checkout \u2192 Customer Contact Method \u2192 Select \"Email\" <br>\nApp Settings & Sales Channels \u2192 Checkout \u2192 Customer information\u2192 in the Full Name option Select \"Require first and last name\u201d and \"Shipping address phone number\".\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_2.png\">\n\n***Turn off automatic order processing***  <br>\nApp settings and sales channels \u2192 General\u2192 Order Processing \u2192 After an order has been paid \u2192 Select \"Don't automatically fulfill any of the line items in the order\"\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_3.png\">\n\n### 2. Configuring the InPost App\nIn the Shopify search bar, please look for InPost.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_6.png\">\n\n***Authentication***\nGo to Setting -> Configuration and insert the credentials provided by InPost.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_7.png\">\n\nDo the same with ***Company information, Return address, Shipments and Pickup Address.*** <br>\n\n***Note \u26a0\ufe0f*** <br>\n- Select a preferred pack dimension between (S \u2013 M \u2013 L) that will be assigned for all shipments creation \n- Please pay attention at the \u201cFlux type\u201d (*In case of any doubts, please contact us) <br>\n    - A2L: Collection from your depot <br>\n    - L2L: Collection from a Locker or InPost Point <br>\n- In Pickup Point, ISO field, please add only the 2 letters country code (es:IT)\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_8.png\">\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_9.png\">\n\n### 3. Carrier Service Set Up\n\nClick on \u201cEnable carrier service\u201d you make InPost available for your client.<br>\n10 is the recommended number of Points (Lockers/InPost Point) to show in the Checkout to give clients a good choice.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Advanced_1.png\">\n\n### 4. Dashboard\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_17.png\">\n\nIn this section orders are collected (a buffer of 5 min is normal from the actual creation) and it\u2019s possible to:\n- Change Box Dimensions\n    - S (P64 x L38 x A8) cm x 25kg\n    - M (P64 x L38 x A19) cm x 25kg \n    - L (P64 x L38 x A39) cm x 25kg\n- Change point (the point can\u2019t be changed after the first currier scan)\n- Generate Labels (Pdf)\n\n- Change point (***\u26a0\ufe0f*** the point can\u2019t be changed after the first currier scan)\n- Generate Labels (Pdf)\n\n### 5. My Shipment\n\nAfter the label is created, the orders pass in this new section where it\u2019s possible to:\n- Print the label again\n- Delate the shipment and so make the order return to the Dashboard\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_18.png\">\n\n# Plus & Basic\n***Shopify InPost Lockers & Pickup Points App*** <br>\nFor Shopify Plus and Shopify Basic Features\n\n## Shopify Basic \u2013 Checkout Preview\n\n- Customers choose Lockers of Pickup Point after the Checkout\n- Possibility to add Map/List after the Checkout.\n- No possibility to filter the distance between Lockers/Points and customer\u2019s address before the\npayment.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_basic_1.png\">\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_basic_2.png\">\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_basic_3.png\">\n\n## Shopify Plus \u2013 Checkout Preview\n\n- Map of List available at the Checkout\n- Customers choose Lockers or Pickup Point before the payment\n- Possibility to add Map od List after the Checkout\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_check_plus.png\">\n\n## App Installation and Configuration\n\nInstall the Plugin from this link: https://apps.shopify.com/inpost-3\n\n### 1. Checkout & Payments Settings on Shopify\n\n***Automatically record payments*** <br>\nApp settings and sales channels \u2192 Payments \u2192 Payment capture method \u2192 Select \"Automatically at checkout\"\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_1.png\">\n\n***Make email / full name / phone entry mandatory*** <br>\nApp Settings & Sales Channels \u2192 Checkout \u2192 Customer Contact Method \u2192 Select \"Email\" <br>\nApp Settings & Sales Channels \u2192 Checkout \u2192 Customer information\u2192 in the Full Name option Select \"Require first and last name\u201d and \"Shipping address phone number\".\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_2.png\">\n\n***Turn off automatic order processing*** <br>\nApp settings and sales channels \u2192 General\u2192 Order Processing \u2192 After an order has been paid \u2192 Select \"Don't automatically fulfill any of the line items in the order\"\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_3.png\">\n\n### 2. Add the InPost Shipping Method on Shopify \n\n***Add an InPost rate at Checkout*** <br>\nGo to Settings -> Shipping & Delivery -> Custom shipping rates, choose the country and click \u201cAdd Rate\u201d.\n- Rate type: Use flat rate\n- Shipping rate: Custom\n- Custom rate name: depends on the country, here some suggestions: \n    - ITA: InPost Lockers 24/7 e Punti di Ritiro \n    - ES/PT: InPost Lockers 24/7 y Punto Pack \n    - FR/BE/LU: Mondial Relay 24/7 et Point Relais \n    - PL/NL: InPost Locker 24/7 and Points\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_4.png\">\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_5.png\">\n\n***Note \u26a0\ufe0f*** <br>\nFor merchants using <span style=\"color:red\">Shopify Basic</span>, we recommend editing the InPost rate filling the \u201cCustom delivery description\u201d (optional field) with this specification: <span style=\"color:red\">\u201cChoose the InPost Locker/Collection Point after payment\u201d</span>.\n\n### 3. Configuring the InPost App\nIn the Shopify search bar, please look for InPost.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_6.png\">\n\n***Authentication*** <br>\nGo to Setting -> Configuration and insert the credentials provided by InPost.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_7.png\">\n\nDo the same with ***Company information, Return address, Shipments and Pickup Address.*** <br>\n\n***Note \u26a0\ufe0f*** <br>\n- Select a preferred pack dimension between (S \u2013 M \u2013 L) that will be assigned for all shipments creation \n- Please pay attention at the \u201cFlux type\u201d (*In case of any doubts, please contact us)\n    - A2L: Collection from your depot\n    - L2L: Collection from a Locker or InPost Point\n- In Pickup Point, ISO field, please add only the 2 letters country code (es:IT)\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_8.png\">\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_9.png\">\n\n### 4. Make InPost live at the Checkout\nFrom the InPost dashboard go on Settings -> Delivery customization, click on \u201cEnable Delivery Customization\u201d button and insert a title (the one you\u2019ll read in the Shopify setting of Delivery) customization.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_10.png\">\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_11.png\">\n\nThe aim of this section is to associate the Shopify Rate to InPost maps. So clicking on \u201cAdd rate\u201d, you first chose how the delivery service is named at the checkout (Shipping method label / Label) and then you select the Rate you previously created on Shopify.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_12.png\">\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_19.png\">\n\n***Note \u26a0\ufe0f*** <br>\nAfter the first setting, if you need to edit the rate name, DON\u2019T do it from Shopify, but only from InPost App in this section.\n\n### 5. \u201cThank you page\u201d setting \u2013 For Shopify Basic ONLY\nBy this set up, customers will see the Maps/List of InPost Lockers and Point after the Chekout/Payment in the Thanks you page. <br>\nGo to Settings -> Checkout -> click on Customize button. Then Click on Checkout and choose \u201cThank you page\u201d. From the left menu, in the Sections part, click on \u201cAdd app block\u201d, choose InPost and Save.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_13.png\">\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_14.png\">\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_15.png\">\n\n### 6. Map in checkout \u2013 For Shopify Plus ONLY\nShopify Plus Merchants can show the List/Map of InPost Lockers and Pickup Points directly in Checkout. Go to Settings -> Checkout -> click on Customize button. <br>\nFrom the left menu, in the Sections part, you can add the InPost Map by clicking at the end of the menu \u201c+Add app block\u201d.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_13.png\">\n\nA new window will be opened and here you can add the InPost Map by clicking at the end of the menu +Add app block.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_16.png\">\n\n### 7. Dashboard\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_17.png\">\n\nIn this section orders are collected (a buffer of 5 min is normal from the actual creation) and it\u2019s possible to:\n- Change Box Dimensions\n    - S (P64 x L38 x A8) cm x 25kg\n    - M (P64 x L38 x A19) cm x 25kg \n    - L (P64 x L38 x A39) cm x 25kg\n- Change point (***\u26a0\ufe0f*** the point can\u2019t be changed after the first currier scan)\n- Generate Labels (Pdf)\n\n### 8. My Shipment\n\nAfter the label is created, the orders pass in this new section where it\u2019s possible to:\n- Print the label again\n- Delate the shipment and so make the order return to the Dashboard\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Shopify_checkout_18.png\">\n\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "Woocommerce",
      "description": "## Installation\nThe plug-in can be downloaded from the site https://inpost.it/soluzioni-le-aziende.\nPlease contact InPost commercial team to activate the service and receive API credentials.\n\nOnce you have the installation file, you can add it to your Wocommerce Store from\n***Plugins  \u2192 Add New***\n\n## Configuration\nOnce installed, the plugin must be configured with the following settings:\n\n\n|ParameterName|Required/Optional |Description |\n|--------------|-----------|---------------|\n|Organization ID |Required |The data must be provided by InPost  |\n|Token            |Required |The data must be provided by InPost  |\n|Type of API     |Required |Sandbox (for testing) or Production  |\n|Company name    |Required |Company name that will be displayed on the shipping label  |\n|Email for delivery notifications |Required |Email used to receive delivery notifications  |\n|Mobile phone for delivery notifications |Required |Mobile Italian phone to receive delivery notifications: <ul><li>Don't use fixed telephone/landline numbers</li><li>The number should always start with a 3</li><li>Non-italian mobile numbers are not accepted</li></ul> |\n|City (Delivery Address for returns to sender)   |Required |City  |\n|Postal code (Delivery Address for returns to sender)      |Required |Postal code  |\n|Street (Delivery Address for returns to sender)           |Required |Street  |\n|Building number (Delivery Address for returns to sender)  |Required |Building number  |\n|Default parcel size |Required |Default parcel size that will be communicated to InPost and which will determine the size of the box to use at the locker. <br>The size can be updated in the order panel.<br> <ul><li>small (8 x 38 x 64 cm)</li><li>medium (19 x 38 x 64 cm) </li><li>large (41 x 38 x 64 cm) </li></ul> |\n|Format of the shipping label |Required |A4 or A6  |\n|Hide the service at the checkout if the total weight is more than 25 Kg |Optional |If checked, InPost delivery method will be hidden at the checkout, preventing parcels from being rejected if the total weight exceeds our maximum allowed value of 25 Kg. This only works if the merchant has entered the weight of each product on their site. |\n|Return Portal link |Optional |Fast Return is an optional InPost service that allows customers to return a parcel in just a few clicks. No API integration is needed. If the service is enabled for the account, enter here the URL of the portal to enable a return button in the Order panel of the User Account.  |\n|Type of flow   |Required |A2L or L2L <br> It will be communicated by InPost|\n|City (Pick Up Address)    |Required ONLY for A2L |City  |\n|Postal code (Pick Up Address)     |Required ONLY for A2L |Postal code  |\n|Street (Pick Up Address)          |Required ONLY for A2L |Street  |\n|Building number (Pick Up Address)  |Required ONLY for A2L |Building number  |\n|Color setting for Inpost call to actions at the checkout |Optional |Set the color of the plugin buttons at the checkout in line with your brand identity.  |\n|Customize the font and styling of the InPost description text at the checkout as per your brand identity |Optional |Set the font and style of the InPost description text at the checkout in line with your brand identity.  |\n\nDon\u2019t forget to add InPost delivery method to a Shipping Zone from ***Setting  \u2192 Shipping***, as well as to assign pricing rules as per Wocommerce standard configurations. \nIt is also possible to decide whether to apply the minimum order rule before or after the discounts. If the \"Apply minimum order rule before coupon discount\" box is checked free shipping would be available based on the pre-discount order amount. Note that this checkbox will only work if you have set up free shipping within the woocommerce shipping methods of the country in question.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/price_setting.png\">\n\nIf there are products that must be excluded from InPost delivery method because too big or too heavy, go to ***Products  \u2192 Edit Product  \u2192 InPost*** and remove the flag \u201cInPost Point 24/7\u201d.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/product_exception.png\">\n\n\n##  InPost order creation at the checkout\n\nThis is an example of how InPost Delivery Method is displayed at the checkout. \n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/Checkout3.png\">\n\nIf InPost delivery method is selected by the customer, it is mandatory to select a collection point from the map. It is possible to search the closest InPost point by city, address, postal code or Point reference. \nNOTE: for testing purposes, use this collection point ITBAR24589 (It can also be modified during the label creation phase - see \"Shipment and label creation\" section).\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/searching.png\">\n\n## InPost post-checkout experience\n\nInPost will send SMS and email notifications to keep both sender and recipient updated about the delivery status.\n\nIf the Fast Return service has been enabled in the plugin configuration, a return button will be visible in the Order area of the User Personal Account. The link will redirect the customer to an external portal. \n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/my_account_order.png\">\n\n## Shipment and label creation\n\nInPost orders are visible both in the Wocommerce Order panel or in ***InPost Italy \u2192 Shipping***.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/order_panel.png\">\n\nFor an Inpost order, the order detail page shows a custom InPost support area from where it is possible to update \n- the collection Point, if requested by the customer\n- the size of the parcel, which by default will be the size configured in the plugin settings. \n- a number reference to be sent to InPost, which by default will be the same of the order number generated by Wocommerce. \nIf the order and shipping data are correct, click \u201cSend Parcel\u201d to create an InPost shipment. \n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/order_panel2.png\">\n\nAfter a few seconds, the \u201cGet Label\u201d button will be available. If used, will generate a shipping label with the format specified in the plugin configuration.\n\n<img src=\"./assets/plugins/order_panel3.png\">\n\nFor bulk operations, there are two options:\n- Go to ***Orders  \u2192 select multiple orders  \u2192 Bulk actions  \u2192 InPost Italy create shipments / InPost Italy create labels***\n- Go to ***InPost Italy  \u2192 Shipments  \u2192 select multiple orders  \u2192 Bulk actions  \u2192 Generate labels***\n\n\n\n\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "MR - Points"
    }
